; The pulsing greybox disc on a trigger zone - a bonfire checkpoint or an arena gate. Replaces two
; identical builders, CheckpointZone.EnsureMarker and GateTravelZone.EnsureMarker, which differed
; only in Modulate (CheckpointLabelColor vs ArenaGateColor). That colour is designer-owned, so it
; stays a binding; the root's name is bound too, because each zone guards on its own marker name.
;
; The pulse owns the transform and the sprite hangs under it, which is how Unity's "two components on
; one marker GameObject" comes apart: there the pulse drove localScale while the renderer owned size,
; and here the sprite's own scale is what carries the size. That order is load-bearing - the pulse
; caches the colour and the scale it finds when it is readied - and it is why this scene is NOT
; merged with AttackReadout.tscn, where the pulse is the child instead.
;
; UNITS: 1 Unity metre = 100 px (World.Ppu). Disc.png is 64x64.
[gd_scene load_steps=3 format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://Scripts/Gameplay/GameplayTelegraphPulse.cs" id="1"]
[ext_resource type="Texture2D" path="res://Resources/Art/Disc.png" id="2"]

[node name="MarkerDisc" type="Node2D"]
; Scale stays 1: this is the pulse's base scale, cached at _Ready, and the sprite below carries size.
script = ExtResource("1")

[node name="Disc" type="Sprite2D" parent="."]
texture = ExtResource("2")
; The zone's own trigger radius sets this per instance: SetSpriteSize(radius * 2) with radius in
; pixels. Authored at WorldTuning.checkpointZoneRadius = 1.5 m -> World.U -> 150 px radius,
; 300 px across, / 64 = 4.6875. A gate binds 1.4 m instead.
scale = Vector2(4.6875, 4.6875)
; GameplayReadabilityDefaults.CheckpointLabelColor as shipped. Designer-owned via
; Resources/Art/Readability.json; a gate binds ArenaGateColor over it.
modulate = Color(0.5176471, 0.57254905, 0.627451, 1)
; SpiritPlatformSortingOrder = 5.
z_index = 5
